WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.763
Welcome.

2
00:00:00.763 --> 00:00:03.707
This briefing comes from
AI Identity Governance,

3
00:00:03.707 --> 00:00:07.012
one of the books of the
Federal Modernization Workbook.

4
00:00:07.012 --> 00:00:10.743
It's written for Chief AI
Officers, CIOs and CISOs,

5
00:00:10.743 --> 00:00:16.525
identity and security operations teams,
ISSOs, and authorizing officials.

6
00:00:16.525 --> 00:00:17.938
I'll take four questions.

7
00:00:17.938 --> 00:00:20.800
Why do AI agents need
identities and owners?

8
00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:22.500
What does governing them involve?

9
00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:24.087
Who owns AI identity?

10
00:00:24.087 --> 00:00:28.487
And how do you scan the inventory and
evidence AI systems for authorization?

11
00:00:28.487 --> 00:00:33.100
The short version: an AI system that
can act is an account with permissions.

12
00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:36.098
Most were deployed outside
the identity program,

13
00:00:36.098 --> 00:00:39.462
and there's no separate AI
authorization to fall back on.

14
00:00:39.462 --> 00:00:41.880
Let's start with what
makes an agent an account.
